          {
            "id": "s_ce9c205cc9",
            "type": "bio",
            "data": {
              "heading": "Our founder",
              "body": "<p>Larkmoor was started by a printer who spent thirty years setting other people&#39;s sentences and wanted, once, to set her own. She still reads every manuscript twice: first walking, then sitting down. The press keeps to two titles a year so that each one can be edited slowly, printed carefully, and sent out with a letter rather than a leaflet.</p>",
              "trustNotes": []
            }
          }
